@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Production deployment and trust boundaries
left to right direction
node "Static HTTPS host\nNo product API" as Host {
  artifact "Versioned shell, .NET runtime,\nWASM, rule profiles, bundle manifests" as Static
}
node "User device" {
  node "Chrome / Edge | application origin" as Browser {
    node "Main browser context" {
      artifact "Blazor C# UI / orchestration\nMemory-only keys and chat" as Main
    }
    node "Dedicated workers" {
      artifact "Rust analysis WASM" as Rust
      artifact "C++ TeX WASM" as TeX
      artifact "C++ PDF WASM" as PDF
      artifact "Storage API glue" as Storage
    }
    node "Service worker" {
      artifact "Versioned shell cache policy" as SW
    }
    database "IndexedDB\nHeads, manifests, metadata" as IDB
    folder "OPFS\nContent objects, bundles, artifacts" as OPFS
    folder "Cache Storage\nApp/runtime assets only" as Cache
  }
  folder "User-selected files / folders" as Files
  node "Local Ollama service\nDownloaded model" as Ollama
}
cloud "Optional online services" {
  node "Google OAuth / Picker / Drive" as Drive
  node "Gemini / Claude APIs" as CloudAI
}
Main --> Rust : revision snapshot
Main --> TeX : project VFS + verified assets
Main --> PDF : compiled artifact
Main --> Storage : repository operations
Storage --> OPFS
Storage --> IDB
Main --> Files : granted picker / ZIP
Main --> Ollama : explicit endpoint
Main --> Drive : explicit transfer / consent
Main --> CloudAI : approved context + BYOK
SW --> Cache
SW --> Static : provision / update only
Main --> SW : shell lifecycle
note bottom of Browser
Workers share origin authority; they are not an XSS sandbox.
Compiler has no network callbacks or provider credentials.
Provisioned local core runs with host/network unavailable.
end note
@enduml
